# D16 applications/user artefacts and D17 desktop/GUI
@phase 1400
[D16-001] FUNC kit 600
cmd: shell_histories
out: shell-history
purpose: Shell and REPL histories of every account incl. root and system accounts: bash, zsh, fish, ash, sh, ksh, tcsh, python, node, mysql, psql, sqlite, redis, less, vim (viminfo), wget-hsts; plus HISTFILE tampering checks.
expect: shell-history/<user>/... copies and history-tampering.txt (HISTFILE=/dev/null, symlinks to /dev/null, zero size, unset in rc files).
empty: EMPTY when no history exists (suspicious for admin accounts).
value: Commands typed by users and attackers; tampering is itself an indicator.
sensitive: yes
ref: draft-13.3; UAC:bash_history

[D16-002] FUNC kit 600
cmd: user_app_artifacts
out: user-apps
purpose: Per user: ~/.aws, ~/.azure, ~/.config/gcloud, ~/.kube, ~/.docker/config.json, ~/.gnupg (key list only), ~/.netrc, ~/.git-credentials, ~/.gitconfig, ~/.config/rclone, FileZilla, ~/.wget-hsts, ~/.npmrc, ~/.pypirc, recently-used.xbel, Trash info.
expect: user-apps/<user>/... copies.
empty: EMPTY when none exist.
value: Cloud and registry credentials an attacker can steal or used to pivot; transfer tool configs used for exfiltration.
sensitive: yes
ref: draft-14.9; draft-31.1

[D16-003] FUNC kit 600
cmd: remote_access_tools
out: remote-access-tools
purpose: Remote access/transfer tools and their logs: AnyDesk, TeamViewer, RustDesk, NoMachine, Chrome Remote Desktop, ScreenConnect, Splashtop, ngrok, frp, chisel, cloudflared, tailscale, rclone, mega, gsutil.
expect: Config/log copies plus found.txt with paths and running state.
empty: EMPTY when none are present.
value: Commercial remote tools and tunnels are a top ransomware access/exfil method.
sensitive: yes
ref: draft-30.3; SANS-FOR577

[D16-004] FUNC kit 300
cmd: dev_tool_artifacts
out: dev-tools
purpose: Configuration and logs of remote IDE servers and notebooks (~/.vscode-server, Jupyter runtime and config).
expect: Copies of settings/log/extension lists (no large caches).
empty: EMPTY when none are present.
value: Remote IDE sessions run commands on the server; tokens and connection details stored on disk.
sensitive: yes
ref: draft-30.3

[D16-005] FUNC kit 120
cmd: tmux_screen_buffers
out: multiplexer
purpose: tmux sessions and paste buffers per user socket; GNU screen sessions and /tmp/screen-exchange.
expect: Session lists and buffer contents.
empty: EMPTY when no tmux/screen runs.
value: Copy/paste buffers and detached attacker sessions.
changes: Talks to the user's tmux server (read-only commands).
sensitive: yes
ref: draft-13.9

@phase 1500
[D17-001] FUNC kit 60
cmd: gui_detect
out: gui-sessions.txt
purpose: Detect graphical sessions: X11 sockets, Wayland sockets, display managers, xrdp/VNC/NoMachine, graphical.target, and the XAUTHORITY of each display.
expect: One line per display/session with owner and auth file.
empty: 'no graphical session' on servers (domain stays NOT_APPLICABLE).
value: Tells which desktop evidence exists.
ref: draft-31.1

[D17-002] FUNC kit 300
cmd: x11_clipboard
out: clipboard
opt: CLIPBOARD
req: ls /tmp/.X11-unix/X* >/dev/null 2>&1
purpose: Clipboard of every X11 display (CLIPBOARD, PRIMARY, SECONDARY; every format; owner PID via X-Resource) with c0f-x11; Wayland via the server's wl-paste when present.
expect: clipboard/<display>/clipboard.tsv and one file per format.
empty: NO_OWNER rows when nothing was copied.
value: Passwords, commands or data an attacker or user just copied.
changes: Creates one temporary InputOnly window; asks the owning application for its data.
sensitive: yes
ref: draft-13.9; draft-40.2

[D17-003] FUNC kit 300
cmd: x11_windows
out: windows
req: ls /tmp/.X11-unix/X* >/dev/null 2>&1
purpose: Window tree of every X11 display: titles, classes, command, geometry, mapped state, owner PID (X-Resource and _NET_WM_PID).
expect: windows/<display>.tsv.
empty: Few windows on idle sessions.
value: What was on screen and which program owns each window.
ref: draft-31.1

[D17-004] FUNC kit 300
cmd: x11_screenshots
out: screenshots
opt: SCREENSHOT
req: ls /tmp/.X11-unix/X* >/dev/null 2>&1
purpose: Screenshot (PNG) of every X11 display.
expect: screenshots/<display>.png.
empty: Locked or blank screens produce dark images.
value: Visual evidence of open applications and attacker activity.
sensitive: yes
ref: draft-31.1

[D17-005] FUNC kit 1800
cmd: browser_artifacts
out: browsers
purpose: Copy browser profiles' evidence files per user: Firefox (places, cookies, formhistory, logins, extensions), Chrome/Chromium/Brave/Edge/Opera/Vivaldi (History, Cookies, Login Data, Web Data, Preferences, Extensions list).
expect: browsers/<user>/<browser>/<profile>/... copies.
empty: EMPTY on servers without browsers.
value: Visited URLs, downloads (malware source), saved logins, malicious extensions.
sensitive: yes
ref: draft-31.1

[D17-006] FUNC kit 1800
cmd: desktop_user_artifacts
out: desktop-users
purpose: Per user: recently-used.xbel, Trash (files + info), thumbnail cache, autostart, GNOME/KDE MRU, keyrings/KWallet files, Thunderbird profile metadata, messengers (Slack/Telegram/Signal/Discord/Teams) config folders without media caches.
expect: desktop-users/<user>/... copies.
empty: EMPTY on servers.
value: Files opened/deleted/viewed (thumbnails survive deletion); communication apps.
sensitive: yes
ref: draft-31.1

[D17-007] COPY kit 600
cmd: -R /var/log/Xorg.*.log /var/log/xrdp*.log /var/log/xrdp-sesman.log /var/log/lightdm /var/log/gdm /var/log/gdm3 /var/log/sddm.log /etc/xrdp /etc/gdm /etc/gdm3 /etc/lightdm /etc/sddm.conf /etc/sddm.conf.d /etc/X11/xorg.conf /etc/X11/xorg.conf.d /etc/tigervnc /etc/vnc /var/lib/AccountsService/users /var/lib/bluetooth /etc/NetworkManager/system-connections /var/lib/udisks2 /var/spool/cups /etc/cups
purpose: Display manager, remote desktop, Bluetooth, Wi-Fi, removable media and printing artefacts.
expect: Logs and configs of the desktop stack.
empty: NOT_FOUND on servers.
value: Remote desktop logins, paired devices, Wi-Fi networks, printed documents.
sensitive: yes
ref: draft-31.1
